  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Normally, combat damage is dealt all at the same time. In that case, Faerie Bladecrafter's first triggered ability triggers once for each player that Faeries you control dealt combat damage to, regardless of how many creatures were dealing that damage. If any of those Faeries have double strike or first strike, the ability will trigger once for each player dealt damage in each combat damage step.",
      "oracle_id": "164b064e-de50-468a-b874-b054897a5be9",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Use Faerie Bladecrafter's power from when it was last on the battlefield to determine the value of X.",
      "oracle_id": "164b064e-de50-468a-b874-b054897a5be9",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Fell Beast of Mordor can't devour creatures entering the battlefield at the same time as it.",
      "oracle_id": "3b64e0a8-7d11-41c5-b439-edec19928b7d",
      "published_at": "2023-11-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Fell Beast of Mordor isn't on the battlefield as its ability resolves, use the number of +1/+1 counters that were on it when it was last on the battlefield to determine the value of X.",
      "oracle_id": "3b64e0a8-7d11-41c5-b439-edec19928b7d",
      "published_at": "2023-11-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Lands are normally colorless permanents, even if they tap for mana of a certain color.",
      "oracle_id": "52244c23-7680-4bed-8ef8-8d10e289d3f7",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The colors are white, blue, black, red, and green. Colorless is not a color.",
      "oracle_id": "52244c23-7680-4bed-8ef8-8d10e289d3f7",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of X is calculated only once, as Shimmercreep's last ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "52244c23-7680-4bed-8ef8-8d10e289d3f7",
      "published_at": "2025-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.",
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2004-12-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".",
      "oracle_id": "60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of X is determined as Valley Rotcaller\u2019s triggered ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "8da0599a-8f63-4dba-857f-b4e10b7191b6",
      "published_at": "2024-07-26",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each creature with lifelink dealing combat damage causes a separate life-gaining event. For example, if two creatures you control with lifelink deal combat damage at the same time, Ajani's Pridemate's ability will trigger twice. However, if a single creature you control with lifelink deals combat damage to multiple creatures, players, planeswalkers, and/or battles at the same time (perhaps because it has trample or was blocked by more than one creature), the ability will trigger only once.",
      "oracle_id": "95e94dea-5ac0-4d6f-adec-ca147aee861f",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Ajani's Pridemate is dealt lethal damage at the same time that you gain life, it won't receive a counter from its ability in time to save it.",
      "oracle_id": "95e94dea-5ac0-4d6f-adec-ca147aee861f",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you gain an amount of life \"for each\" of something or \"equal to the number\" of something, that life is gained as one event and Ajani's Pridemate's ability triggers only once.",
      "oracle_id": "95e94dea-5ac0-4d6f-adec-ca147aee861f",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In a Two-Headed Giant game, life gained by your teammate won't cause Ajani's Pridemate's ability to trigger, even though it caused your team's life total to increase.",
      "oracle_id": "95e94dea-5ac0-4d6f-adec-ca147aee861f",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ability of Ajani's Pridemate triggers just once for each life-gaining event, whether it's 1 life from Dazzling Angel or 4 life from Apothecary Stomper.",
      "oracle_id": "95e94dea-5ac0-4d6f-adec-ca147aee861f",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.",
      "oracle_id": "9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744",
      "published_at": "2019-07-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.",
      "oracle_id": "9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744",
      "published_at": "2019-07-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
